---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const PALETTE = [
  { name: "Ground", hex: "#1b140c" },
  { name: "Accent", hex: "#ffaa3c" },
  { name: "Secondary", hex: "#ffc46e" },
  { name: "Head", hex: "#ffffff" },
];
---
<Base
  title="The Bead Reserve : Brand Assets"
  description="Logo files, palette, and terms of use for the BEADZ reserve seal."
>
  <header class="masthead">
    <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--amber-mid)">Press &amp; Third-Party Use</div>
    <h1>The Bead <em>Reserve</em> : Brand Assets</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--text-soft);font-size:clamp(16px,1.6vw,19px)">
      Logo files, palette, and terms of use for the BEADZ reserve seal. Take them from here rather
      than lifting a screenshot. There is one mark, and no wordmark or alternate lockup.
    </p>
    <p class="mono" style="margin-top:12px;font-size:13px">
      <a href="/">&larr;&nbsp;The Bead Reserve</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="mark-heading" style="margin:0 0 40px">
    <h2 id="mark-heading" class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--text-soft);font-size:12px">The Mark</h2>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(160px,220px) 1fr;gap:28px;align-items:start;margin-top:12px">
      <div style="background:#1b140c;border:2px solid var(--line);padding:20px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center">
        <img
          src="/beadz-seal.svg"
          alt="The Bead Reserve seal: a circular mark reading THE BEAD RESERVE around the top rim, Henry the robot mascot at the center, and 47,318 / ERC-20 · BASE lettered flat beneath"
          width="220"
          height="220"
          style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <p style="margin-top:0">
          The seal has a dark ground. Put it on a dark surface, as shown here, rather than straight
          onto white.
        </p>
        <table class="mono" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;margin-top:8px">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="text-align:left;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line);padding:8px 10px 8px 0">File</th>
              <th style="text-align:left;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line);padding:8px 10px">Format</th>
              <th style="text-align:left;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line);padding:8px 10px">Use</th>
              <th style="text-align:left;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line);padding:8px 0"></th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">beadz-token-512.png</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">PNG, 512×512</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">General logo use, app icons</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">
                <a href="/beadz-token-512.png" download>Download</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">beadz-token-256.png</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">PNG, 256×256</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">Token lists, wallets</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">
                <a href="/beadz-token-256.png" download>Download</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0">beadz-seal.svg</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px">SVG, vector</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 10px">Print, press, anything that needs to scale</td>
              <td style="padding:8px 0">
                <a href="/beadz-seal.svg" download>Download</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="permanence-heading" style="margin:0 0 40px">
    <h2 id="permanence-heading" class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--text-soft);font-size:12px">Permanence</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:12px">
      These URLs are canonical and will not change. Listing sites and press hard-code asset links and
      rarely re-fetch, so link to them directly rather than mirroring a copy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="palette-heading" style="margin:0 0 40px">
    <h2 id="palette-heading" class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--text-soft);font-size:12px">Palette</h2>
    <table class="mono" style="width:100%;max-width:480px;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;margin-top:12px">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="text-align:left;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line);padding:8px 10px 8px 0"></th>
          <th style="text-align:left;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line);padding:8px 10px">Role</th>
          <th style="text-align:left;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line);padding:8px 10px">Hex</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {PALETTE.map((c) => (
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:8px 10px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                style={`display:inline-block;width:18px;height:18px;border:2px solid var(--line);background:${c.hex};vertical-align:middle`}
              ></span>
            </td>
            <td style="padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">{c.name}</td>
            <td style="padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">{c.hex}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="usage-heading" style="margin:0 0 40px">
    <h2 id="usage-heading" class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--text-soft);font-size:12px">Usage Rules</h2>
    <ul style="margin-top:12px;padding-left:20px">
      <li>Don't stretch, rotate, or recolor the mark.</li>
      <li>Don't separate Henry from the seal, or use him alone as a mark.</li>
      <li>Don't redraw the mark. Use the supplied files.</li>
      <li>
        The mark needs about 96px to stay legible. Below that, use the favicon files
        (<code class="mono">favicon-16x16.png</code>, <code class="mono">favicon-32x32.png</code>,
        <code class="mono">beadz-seal-small.svg</code>), which are drawn separately for small sizes
        rather than scaled down.
      </li>
      <li>Don't crowd the rim with other text or graphics.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="licensing-heading" style="margin:0 0 40px">
    <h2 id="licensing-heading" class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--text-soft);font-size:12px">Licensing</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:12px">
      The BEADZ software is MIT-licensed, and forking it is encouraged. Deploy your own vault, reserve
      your own beads. Henry and the reserve seal are the one carve-out from that grant: they are
      © Curt Henrichs, all rights reserved, under the BRAND ASSETS EXCEPTION in the repository's
      <code class="mono">LICENSE</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may use this mark to <em>refer to</em> The Bead Reserve, in an article, a listing, or a
      token-list entry. You may not use it as the identity of your own project, including a fork of
      this one. A fork is expected to swap in its own mark. Nothing in the software depends on this one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="counterfeit-heading">
    <h2 id="counterfeit-heading" class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--text-soft);font-size:12px">Counterfeits</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:12px">
      The Bead Reserve seeds no liquidity pool and never will. Any BEADZ token that can be bought on an
      exchange is, by construction, not this project. If you see this mark used to promote a purchasable
      token, that use is not endorsed by The Bead Reserve.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
